{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfs6ppx16qvsLy2S6dek2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Version-specific `pre_built` and `wheel_server_url` now carry through the START phase, and both test files pass (222 tests, run with `.venv/bin/python -m pytest -o addopts=`). I haven't committed anything. The full suite and the e2e tests were not run.\n\n**What changed**\n- **`_pbi.py`:**\n  - `is_pre_built(version)` and `get_wheel_server_url(version)` strip the local segment with `Version(version.public)` before the lookup.\n  - `is_pre_built` calls the hook through `overrides.find_and_invoke` only when a version is given, and a non-None hook result wins over YAML. The module-level `_default_is_pre_built` returns `None`.\n  - The `pre_built` and `wheel_server_url` properties delegate to those methods with no version.\n  - The `versionadded` directives are bumped to 0.95.0.\n- **`_models.py`:** no edit was needed. A bare `versions:` key already becomes an empty mapping, and an omitted key already defaults to one.\n- **`wheels.py`:** no edit was needed. `get_wheel_server_urls` already accepted `version=None` and used the version-specific URL when given.\n- **`_start.py`:**\n  - I added `_re_resolve_url` with the signature and behaviour you described.\n  - START re-resolves right after `pbi_pre_built` is set, using the re-resolve conditions you gave, and logs INFO before and a WARNING if it keeps the original URL. This runs before the graph add and before the has-been-seen check.\n- **Docs:** I added a section on the `is_pre_built` hook to `hooks-and-overrides.rst` and a paragraph on version-specific settings to `package-settings.rst`.\n- **Tests:** new tests cover the local-version lookup, the hook, bare `versions:`, `_re_resolve_url`, the re-resolve cases, the failure fallback, and a second parent of an already-seen package. In the existing `test_sets_pbi_pre_built_before_prepare_source` I added `wheel_server_url` and `get_wheel_server_url` to its Mock. Without that it would now trigger a re-resolve.\n\n**Two things to check**\n- In the source branch I catch only `ResolverException` and return `None` for an empty result. You didn't say which exceptions should map to `None`, so tell me if you want it broader.\n- `mypy` reports two errors in `src/fromager/resolver.py` (lines 1219 and 1342). I didn't touch that file, so I take these to be pre-existing and left them."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1307,"cache_read_input_tokens":127812,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1307},"output_tokens":746,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"97ddeb5e-36cf-4ab2-ab92-86345dca8664","uuid":"82fe1f93-a0c6-4a3c-b5d1-e4ba09c92917","timestamp":"2026-10-09T18:01:36.867Z","request_id":"req_011Cfs6pphrwm2xfab9BmaC2"}
